{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SyDeKRGmi1UqRm8UooWUFm","type":"tool_result","content":"    min: 1,\n    class: 'qty',\n    onChange: (ev:CustomEvent) => setQty(ev.detail),\n})\n```\n\nIn the browser, the host gets a `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` that never\nchanges once the host is in the document. While hydrating, Preact\nleaves that element's children alone, so the element adopts the server\nmarkup. Later renders never write `innerHTML` either.\n\n**Client-only render.** With no server markup, call Preact's `render`.\nOn that first render the adapter fills the host with the component's\ninner HTML from its `renderParts` static, before the element connects,\nso the element finds its markup and refs. This needs the variant of\nthe component that keeps its render link, with\n[`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) loaded (the\nbuild transform imports it for a kept render link). A component whose\nrender link was stripped mounts as an empty host.\n\n```ts\nimport { h, render } from 'preact'\n\nrender(h(PreactNumberInput, { min: 1 }), document.body)\n```\n\n**Two builds.** The import resolves by export condition, the same way\nas [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm). The `browser` condition selects a\nbuild that contains no render code. The default build, for Node and\nSSR, imports [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support).\n\n77:  * [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support)\n836:import [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) once.\n1492:### `microtags/render-support`","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c0eb7c9-4c49-4c5f-bbb4-d093463c7645","uuid":"c3c1b5cc-4307-4dfb-9bdf-5e34ea8805d2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:28:11.656Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"    min: 1,\n    class: 'qty',\n    onChange: (ev:CustomEvent) => setQty(ev.detail),\n})\n```\n\nIn the browser, the host gets a `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` that never\nchanges once the host is in the document. While hydrating, Preact\nleaves that element's children alone, so the element adopts the server\nmarkup. Later renders never write `innerHTML` either.\n\n**Client-only render.** With no server markup, call Preact's `render`.\nOn that first render the adapter fills the host with the component's\ninner HTML from its `renderParts` static, before the element connects,\nso the element finds its markup and refs. This needs the variant of\nthe component that keeps its render link, with\n[`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) loaded (the\nbuild transform imports it for a kept render link). A component whose\nrender link was stripped mounts as an empty host.\n\n```ts\nimport { h, render } from 'preact'\n\nrender(h(PreactNumberInput, { min: 1 }), document.body)\n```\n\n**Two builds.** The import resolves by export condition, the same way\nas [`microtags/htm`](#microtagshtm). The `browser` condition selects a\nbuild that contains no render code. The default build, for Node and\nSSR, imports [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support).\n\n77:  * [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support)\n836:import [`microtags/render-support`](#microtagsrender-support) once.\n1492:### `microtags/render-support`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/microtags.review-fix/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1563,"oldLines":15,"newStart":1563,"newLines":19,"lines":[" })"," ```"," ","-In the browser, the host gets a fixed, empty `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.","-While hydrating, Preact leaves that element's children alone, so the","-element adopts the server markup. Because the value never changes,","-later renders never write `innerHTML` either.","+In the browser, the host gets a `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` that never","+changes once the host is in the document. While hydrating, Preact","+leaves that element's children alone, so the element adopts the server","+markup. Later 