{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M43VYQStQbuoBtvmouFxar","type":"tool_result","content":"`src/preact.browser.ts` is selected by the `browser` condition (listed\nfirst in `exports[\"./preact\"]`). It passes declared props and\npassthrough attrs as vnode props, `on<event-name>` per mapped event,\nand one shared module constant `{ __html: '' }` as\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; a fresh object per render would still work\nbut the shared one documents the contract. Its `build-esm:min` entry\nrelies on `--external:preact` (that flag applies to every min entry)\nand its size entry uses `ignore: ['preact']`. Because the root\ntypecheck sets the `browser` condition, `'microtags/preact'` in\n`test/types.ts` is the browser build; compare it with\n`'../dist/preact.js'` (dist and src declarations are distinct types,\nso never compare a dist type with a src one). Browser tests live in\n`test/preact-browser.ts` (imported by `test/index.ts`). Core does not\nrender into an empty host on connect, so a test component that must\nwork client-only renders its own markup in setup and has no refs\n(refs are collected before setup). htm needs void tags self-closed\n(`<input />`) or the render static emits `input[object Object]`.\n`npm run test:bundles` (`test/bundles.ts`, needs `dist/`) holds the\n`MARKERS` table: fixed strings that must not appear in listed built\nfiles, each first found in a control (else \"stale\"). Entries are read\nwith their split chunks (render support's code lives in a chunk, not\n`dist/render-support.js`); a new `dist` entry belongs in its lists.\n\n### CLI entry (`src/cli.ts`)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c0eb7c9-4c49-4c5f-bbb4-d093463c7645","uuid":"7cdb5fb5-79e3-40ee-8352-205c5e94e7c9","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:28:13.946Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"`src/preact.browser.ts` is selected by the `browser` condition (listed\nfirst in `exports[\"./preact\"]`). It passes declared props and\npasst