{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrt3vmJquPZfBstNoPxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NVTJyAGX9zE7y3iKrvDtju","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p .nightralph && cat > .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Review-fix notes\n\n## Finding 1: client-only render leaves host empty -- DONE\n- Fixed in the adapter (not core): `src/preact.browser.ts` keeps one\n  `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` object per component instance (`useRef` from\n  `preact/hooks`). Its `__html` getter returns `renderParts(own, {attrs})`\n  html until the host's ref fires (host committed), then a fixed value.\n  Preact never reads `__html` while hydrating (diff/index.js\n  `!isHydrating && ...`), so it is read before commit only on a\n  client-only mount, and innerHTML is set before the element connects.\n- Test fixture in test/preact-browser.ts no longer renders in setup; it\n  uses refs (`r.one`). Client-only + events tests failed red before.\n- Size: browser adapter 443 -> 564 B; limit raised 450 -> 600 B.\n- Docs: README Preact section, ADR-010 decision/consequences, AGENTS.md.\n- Client-only mount requires render support registered (full variant\n  via the build transform); otherwise renderParts throws naming subpath.\nEOF\ngit add -A -- . ':!.nightralph' && git commit -qm \"preact browser adapter: render inner HTML on a client-only mount\n\nCore never renders into an empty host, so a client-only Preact render\nleft real components empty. The adapter now keeps one\ndangerouslySetInnerHTML per instance whose __html comes from\nrenderParts until the host is committed, then never changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":573,"cache_read_input_tokens":90188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"