{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgrt8Eq81c4tBXfiYR5tY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RWVGShtHTMVVvvXX6pZZ1y","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='docs/adr/ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''  render record contract is unchanged, so any copy of core keeps\n  working with any copy of render support.\n'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,old+'''- `renderHost` now builds its string from the parts, whose `attrs` is a\n  record, so a name appears once. When an extra attr has the same name\n  as a declared prop that serializes, the host carries only the\n  declared value: `render({ n: 1 }, { attrs: { n: '2' } })` gives\n  `<x n=\"1\">`, where 0.0.14 gave `<x n=\"1\" n=\"2\">`. An HTML parser\n  keeps the first of a duplicate, so the parsed DOM is the same; only\n  the bytes change. A declared prop that is unset, null or prop-only\n  leaves the extra attr in place.\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngit add -A && git commit -qm \"render: record that a declared prop wins over a same-name extra attr\n\nPins the deduplication renderHost gained when it moved onto render\nparts, and records it in ADR-010.\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: render() no longer emits an extra attr whose name\nmatches a declared prop that serializes; render({ n: 1 }, { attrs:\n{ n: '2' } }) now gives <x n=\\\"1\\\"> instead of <x n=\\\"1\\\" n=\\\"2\\\">.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\" && git log --oneline -1\ncat >> .nightralph/notes.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Finding 3: renderHost not byte-identical on same-name extra attr -- DONE\n- Read as \"unrecorded behavior change\": kept the new (dedupe) behavior,\n  since parts.attrs is a record and the parsed DOM is unchanged.\n- Pinned with `render: a declared prop wins over an extra attr of its\n  name` in test/ssr.ts (passes on current code; there was no red step\n  because the code was not wrong, only undocu