{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrtB5eYM4UuUAWAgeTiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three findings are fixed and committed in four commits on `microtags--review-fix`. The final gate passed: lint is clean, `npm test` passes 458/458, `test:ssr` 130/130, `test:preact-ssr` 15/15 and `test:bundles` 28/28.\n\n1. **Client-only render left the host empty** (`241751c`). I fixed this in the browser adapter, not in core. Each component instance now keeps one `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` object, held with `useRef` from `preact/hooks`. Its `__html` getter returns the HTML from `El.renderParts(...)` until the host is first committed, and after that the value never changes. Preact never reads `__html` while hydrating, so it is only read before commit on a client-only mount. That puts the markup in place before the element connects, so setup finds its refs.\n   - I rewrote the test fixture so it only reads refs and renders nothing in setup. With the old adapter, the client-only and events tests failed with \"missing refs\"; they pass now.\n   - The browser adapter grew from 443 B to 585 B, so I raised its size limit from 450 B to 600 B.\n   - README, ADR-010 and AGENTS.md now describe how this works.\n   - A client-only mount needs the variant of the component that keeps its render link, with render support loaded. The build transform adds that import for a kept render link. A component whose render link was stripped still mounts as an empty host.\n\n2. **Declared props were lost during `hydrate`** (`f7edee4`). The host gets a new ref callback on every render, so Preact calls it on every commit. It assigns each declared prop whose value differs from what the element holds. Functions are skipped, because Preact already sets those while hydrating. A new test hydrates with a list passed to a prop-only prop and checks it after hydrate, after a re-render with the same list, and after a new list. It failed before the fix and passes now. README and ADR-010 are updated.\n\n3. **`renderHost` output changed when an extra attr has a declared prop's name** (`37b8743`, plus `4b57a78` for a typecheck fix in the test). I kept the new behaviour, where only the declared value is emitted. The parts store attributes as a record, so a name can only appear once, and a browser keeps the first of two duplicate attributes, so the resulting DOM is unchanged. A new SSR test covers this, and ADR-010 now records the change. I didn't edit `CHANGELOG.md` by hand because the `version` script regenerates it from git history. Instead, the commit carries a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer so the change lands in the 0.1.0 changelog. Unlike the first two, this fix had no failing-test step: the code wasn't wrong, the change just wasn't written down.\n\nMy notes for this attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which git ignores and which I did not commit.\n\n[x] Client-only Preact render leaves a real component's host empty; README/ADR-010 promise it renders itself, and the test hides this with a hand-written setup\n[x] Declared props are never assigned to the element during `hydrate`, so prop-only (and any non-attribute) values passed through the adapter are lost\n[x] `renderHost` output is no longer byte-identical when an extra attr has the same name as a declared prop"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274,"cache_read_input_tokens":100690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c0eb7c9-4c49-4c5f-bbb4-d093463c7645","uuid":"88081984-23bc-49f0-a2e9-c45f9b92cffc","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:30:13.745Z","request_id":"req_011CgrtB5RA6MGD3aogcMeqb"}
